<article class="env-corollary" id="069C">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/069C">Corollary <span data-tag="069C">4.4.3.21</span> <span class="named">(Slices of Isofibrations)</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an isofibration of $\infty $-categories. Then, for every diagram $f: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the induced map of slice $\infty $-categories $U_{/f}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/f} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ / (U \circ f)}$ is also an isofibration. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor $U_{/f}$ factors as a composition 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/f} \xrightarrow {T} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ / (U \circ f) } \xrightarrow {U'} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ / (U \circ f) } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $T$ is a right fibration (Proposition <a data-tag="01BZ" href="/tag/01BZ">4.3.6.8</a>) and $U'$ is a pullback of $U$. Example <a data-tag="01EW" href="/tag/01EW">4.4.1.11</a> guarantees that $T$ is an isofibration, and Corollary <a data-tag="01H4" href="/tag/01H4">4.4.3.19</a> guarantees that $U'$ is an isofibration. Applying Remark <a data-tag="01GW" href="/tag/01GW">4.4.1.10</a>, we conclude that $U_{/f} = U' \circ T$ is an isofibration. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
